; THE EMBERMARKET — "the Coilyard" (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild). The Ember Crown's trade district, one street
; south of the town square, and as of this phase a district you navigate rather than a street you walk
; down.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT THIS REPLACED, AND WHY THE OLD SHAPE IS NOT COMING BACK. 38K/38L built a forecourt, a
; straight 7 m central spine, two mirrored stall rows at x = ±9, a plaza off to the west and a bell
; tower centred on the far end of the axis. It read at a glance and it read the same at every glance:
; one entrance, one decision, and every stall visible from the threshold. A market is the one place in
; a realm that should be hard to see the end of.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW — three entrances of three different characters, and a route that bends four times
; between the first and the last of them:
;
;   NORTH, the Gate Lane      x -13.25..-8.75, z -26..-13. A 4.5 m slot between HouseW1 and HouseE1,
;                             braziers on both jambs and banners overhead. This is the way in from the
;                             town square and it is deliberately the tightest ground in the realm: you
;                             arrive compressed, and you cannot see the market at all from the seam.
;   the bend                  z -13..-8. StallX1 narrows it further from the west; the notice board is
;                             on the east wall where a person entering will actually read it.
;   the Crookway              a 5 m lane on a -24° bearing from the bend to (2, -7.5), stalls packed
;                             along it. Still enclosed. Still no sightline to the yard.
;   THE COIL YARD             x -4..18, z -8..12 — 22 x 20 m, and the reveal the first 20 m exists to
;                             set up. It opens on the LEFT of the Crookway's exit, which is why the
;                             lane is angled rather than straight: a straight lane reveals the yard
;                             gradually, a bent one hands it over all at once.
;   EAST, the Caravan Road    x 16..26, z 0.25..6.75. Seven metres wide, cart-scaled, the opposite of
;                             the north gate. Sera's waggon and the consignment desk stand on it.
;   WEST, the Dock Stair      x -26..-18, z 10.25..13.75. A 3.5 m back way in from Hollowreach that
;                             does not touch the yard at all — it feeds the alley.
;   Netmenders' Alley         x -19.6..-16.4, z -15..15. A 3.2 m service run BEHIND the west frontage,
;                             connecting the dock stair to the gate lane's west side. Nothing sells on
;                             it. It is the shortcut you learn, and the only route with no stalls.
;   the Salt Steps            x 10.5..21.5, z 9..19 — a 0.3 m terrace on the yard's south-east with
;                             the well, three benches and THE BELL TOWER ON TOP OF IT. A tower on a
;                             terrace is the silhouette you catch over the north roofs from the square.
;   Sump Court                x -16..-7, z 13..21. A dead end off the alley: the cook-fire, a brazier
;                             and nothing to buy. Somewhere to find rather than somewhere to pass.
;   the Timber Yard           x -4..10, z 12..21. The joiner's working ground, south of the yard.
;
; ⚠️ THE STALL TRANSFORMS MOVED, AND THE OLD COMMENT SAYING THEY COULD NOT IS GONE. 38K promised 38L
; that placing a merchant would be "a transform copied out of this file", and that promise was kept by
; freezing x = ±9 / z = -14, -3, +8 — which is exactly how a district gets stuck. What was actually
; load-bearing is the SHAPE of the contract, not its coordinates: every stall still carries its Counter
; at local (2.2, 0, 0), and every merchant still stands at stall + 1.1 m along the stall's own +X,
; facing back down it. Both survive any move, because both are relative. The eleven schedules under
; data/schedules/Embermarket*.tres were migrated with this rebuild — they are cell-local against
; Origin (0, 0, 46), so each destination is the new stall position, not the old one.
;
; ⚠️ STALL BEARINGS ARE THE POINT. Nothing in this cell shares a bearing with the thing next to it
; except where a group is deliberately a row of two. The yaw convention: a stall's +X is its CUSTOMER
; side, so yaw 270 faces its counter north, 90 south, 0 east, 180 west. A merchant's yaw is her
; stall's + 90 (a body faces its own -Z).
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav. Geometry outside the NavigationRegion3D is not carved into the
; navmesh, so an NPC or an enemy walks straight through a stall that looks solid. NPCs and the notice
; board deliberately do NOT (see the actor block at the bottom) — only static geometry should carve.
;
; ⚠️ The cell is placed at its Center by the RegionStreamer, so every transform in this file is LOCAL to
; the market's own origin. The 37C placement bug — a point read out of a .tscn landing a cell's width
; from where it was authored — is the same mistake in the other direction.
;
; ⚠️ THE SALT STEPS ARE THE ONLY RAISED GROUND IN THE REALM (39C, moved here in 44). 0.3 m, inside
; StepUp.MaxHeight (0.5) and exactly ON the navmesh's agent_max_climb (0.3 — one voxel of this
; cell's 0.3 cell_height), so the player and every NPC reach it by the same rule. The well, the three benches and the bell tower ride 0.3 m up with it — a
; prop left at y = 0 would be sunk to its ankles. EVERY OTHER GROUND SLAB HERE IS A 5-6 CM SKIN WITH NO
; COLLIDER: a 6 cm lip is beneath the step-up's minimum and is something the player catches on rather
; than climbs. Raised ground is possible; it is not therefore free.
;
; ⚠️ ELEVEN BUILDINGS WERE ADDED AND THEY ARE STRUCTURE, NOT SCENERY. BlockNorth, BlockSouth and
; BlockWest form the island the Gate Lane runs down one side of and the alley the other. Delete them
; and there is no lane — only an open field with stalls in it, which is the layout this rebuild
; replaced.

; ⚠️ THE NAV VOXEL GRID COARSENED WITH THE WORLD (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Cells
; went from 52 m squares on a flat slab to 90-200 m of real terrain, and a 0.25 m voxel over
; five times the area is twenty-five times the columns to rasterise — the traversal probe timed
; out waiting for the bake. ⚠️ AND THE agent_* DIMS DID NOT FOLLOW. On the 0.25 grid 1.75 and
; 0.5 were whole voxels; on this one they are not, so every bake quantised them and warned. The
; values below are the QUANTISED ones, so the file now says what the bake does: agent_height and
; agent_radius CEIL to a voxel (cell_height / cell_size), agent_max_climb FLOORS to cell_height.
; ⚠️ They encode this grid — change cell_size or cell_height and recompute all three with it.
[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="BoxMesh_salt_steps"]
size = Vector3(11, 0.3, 10)

[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_particle_ember"]
transparency = 1
shading_mode = 0
