; --- Brightcut's Scales (Phase 38P2) --------------------------------------------------------------
; The appraiser: Nessa's assay counter, at the end of her stall. Same shape as MarketNotice above -
; an Entity with a mesh, a collider and exactly one interactable component.
;
; ⚠️ A SEPARATE ENTITY FROM NESSA, AND FORCED. She carries a DialogueComponent and an entity gets one
; interactable, so a ServiceComponent on her would never fire. Her talk line now points at this.
;
; ⚠️ prp_tome_stand WAS TRIED HERE FIRST AND REJECTED ON SIGHT. It renders as a grey stone plinth -
; correct for the Ancient Aerie it was adopted for, and a temple monument parked among timber stalls
; here. A table is the market's own material and reads as her counter, which is what her line says.
;
; ⚠️ COLLIDER MEASURED, AND MEASURING THE ACCESSORS IS NOT ENOUGH. prp_tome_stand's POSITION min/max
; say 1.743 x 2.315 x 1.743, but its single node carries scale 0.527, so the real prop is 0.92 x 1.22
; - the first collider authored here was over twice too big in every axis and would have been an
; invisible wall. prp_table_large has NO node scale, so its 2.848 x 0.813 x 1.097 is the real size.
; Apply node scale to a measured bounding box, or the number is fiction.

[node name="BrightcutScales" type="Node3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(-0.9397, 0, -0.342, 0, 1, 0, 0.342, 0, -0.9397, 15, 0, -1)
script = ExtResource("2_entity")
DisplayName = "Brightcut's Scales"

